eat Intelligence Group. (2026, May 11). GTIG AI Threat Tracker: Adversaries Leverage AI for Vulnerability Exploitation, Augmented Operations, and Initial Access. Retrieved July 7, 2026.", "source_name": "Google AI Threat Tracker MAY 2026", "url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/ai-vulnerability-exploitation-initial-access"}, {"description": "Hunt.io. (2026, May 14). How TeamPCP''s Python Toolkit Survives a C2 Takedown: FIRESCALE, GitHub, and the Victim''s Own Account. Retrieved July 16, 2026.", "source_name": "Hunt.io TeamPCP Toolkit MAY 2026", "url": "https://hunt.io/blog/teampcp-python-toolkit-firescale-github-c2-takedown"}, {"description": "McCarthy, R. (2026, March 20). Trivy Compromised: Everything You Need to Know about the Latest Supply Chain Attack. Retrieved July 1, 2026.", "source_name": "Wiz Trivy Compromise MAR 2026", "url": "https://www.wiz.io/blog/trivy-compromised-teampcp-supply-chain-attack"}, {"description": "McCarthy, R., Cohen, A., and Read, B. (2026, May 12). Mini Shai-Hulud Strikes Again: TanStack + more npm Packages Compromised. Retrieved July 16, 2026.", "source_name": "Wiz Mini Shai-Hulud MAY 2026", "url": "https://www.wiz.io/blog/mini-shai-hulud-strikes-again-tanstack-more-npm-packages-compromised"}, {"description": "McCarthy, R., Haughom, J., Read, B. (2026, March 23). KICS GitHub Action Compromised: TeamPCP Strikes Again in Supply Chain Attack. Retrieved July 1, 2026.", "source_name": "Wiz TeamPCP KICS MAR 2026", "url": "https://www.wiz.io/blog/teampcp-attack-kics-github-action"}, {"description": "Santos, J. and Navato, J.R. (2026, May 13). Analyzing TeamPCP’s Supply Chain Attacks: Checkmarx KICS and elementary-data in CI/CD Credential Theft. Retrieved July 16, 2026.", "source_name": "Trend Micro TeamPCP MAY 2026", "url": "https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/e/analyzing-teampcp-supply-chain-attacks.html"}, {"description": "Unit 42. (2026, March 31). Weaponizing the Protectors: TeamPCP’s Multi-Stage Supply